<article class="env-lemma" id="0AS4">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AS4">Lemma <span data-tag="0AS4">10.50.6</span>.</a> Let $I$ be a directed set. Let $(A_ i, \varphi _{ij})$ be a system of valuation rings over $I$. Then $A = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits A_ i$ is a valuation ring. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is clear that $A$ is a domain. Let $a, b \in A$. Lemma <a href="/tag/052K" data-tag="052K">10.50.5</a> tells us we have to show that either $a | b$ or $b | a$ in $A$. Choose $i$ so large that there exist $a_ i, b_ i \in A_ i$ mapping to $a, b$. Then Lemma <a href="/tag/00IB" data-tag="00IB">10.50.4</a> applied to $a_ i, b_ i$ in $A_ i$ implies the result for $a, b$ in $A$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>